{:edb/db-before-t 12990 :edb/db-after-t 12991 :edb/tx-data [[13194139546303 50 #inst "2026-11-04T20:38:27.791Z" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186059672 1038 #edb/ref 17592186749685 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186059672 1038 #edb/ref 17592186749688 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186059672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186749271 13194139546303 17592186576411 false] [17592186059672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186749695 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749214 1173 true 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749226 1173 true 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749243 1173 true 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749269 1173 true 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749685 1068 #edb/ref 17592186749694 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749685 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749685 1071 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n\\frac{\\sec\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)}{\\sin\\left(33.75^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(33.75^\\circ\\right)}.\n$$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749685 1072 #uuid "018e9f50-0472-569b-869e-52327dfb3a0b" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749685 1074 "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Apply $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ at $x=33.75^\\circ$ in the denominator. Use $\\sec x=1/\\cos x$, then apply the double-angle identity again at $x=67.5^\\circ$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{2\\,\\sec\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)}{\\sin\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)}\\\\&=\\frac{2}{\\sin\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)}\\\\&=\\frac{4}{\\sin\\left(135^\\circ\\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(135^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nRationalize the denominator by multiplying numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2}$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{4}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}\\\\&=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\&=4 \\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749686 1080 "4 \\sqrt{2}" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749686 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749686 1083 #uuid "250ff5c2-1fcc-5eba-b50b-aeefc4d78e4f" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749687 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749687 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749687 1083 #uuid "2d017e70-2af1-54e6-9041-60add084bf85" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749688 1068 #edb/ref 17592186749689 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749688 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749688 1071 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n4\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right).\n$$" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749688 1072 #uuid "47b7e499-be75-5994-89eb-47a2f5bdc3dc" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749688 1074 "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{16}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186749687 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186749690 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186749691 13194139546303 17592186576411 true] [17592186749689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186749692 13194139546303 17592186576411 tr